Taxonomy
Nymphaea gigantea was first described in 1852 by the English botanist and illustrator William Jackson Hooker in The Botanical Magazine, based on material collected by John Carne Bidwill from the Wide Bay area of Queensland (at that time still a part of the colony of New South Wales). The description was accompanied by an illustration by Walter Hood Fitch detailing the flower.{{R|APNI|BotMag1852|Whittell}}
It is placed in the subgenus Nymphaea subg. Anecphya.
